diff --git a/tests/module_lifecycle/README.md b/tests/module_lifecycle/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c26e43c9e3d2cde8c6402ccaffef0c7d2e40f0c3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/module_lifecycle/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Module lifecycle regression
+
+`python3 tests/module_lifecycle/run.py [--sanitizers]` compiles the production
+controller, module notifier, deferred worker and feature exit with explicit
+host models for kernel APIs. It exercises late loads, COMING/LIVE transitions,
+GOING, reloads with a new inode identity, unrelated modules, pending-name
+remapping, events during work, registration failures and shutdown admission.
+
+Automatic-discovery cases additionally cover sorted stock exclusion, effective
+root visibility, transactional inventory failure, an already-loaded snapshot,
+unload/reload, an event during a path lookup, manual-rule overlap, a changed
+stock inventory and bounded-registry overflow.
+
+Six compiled mutations must fail: lost manual/automatic events, incorrect stock
+classification, wrong name remapping, missing notifier unregistration and
+missing work cancellation. Filesystem operations
+assert process context and the configuration mutex; unregister/cancel assert
+that the mutex is not held. This does not replace a real-kernel load/reload or
+unload test and does not measure the deferred sysfs visibility window.
